{"_comment": "Nonimmigrant ADMISSIONS by class of admission and year (DHS Yearbook table 25), with admissions by class and destination state (supplemental table 3). Built because there is NO EMPLOYER-LEVEL DATA FOR L-1 OR O-1: neither requires a labour condition application and USCIS publishes no employer hub for either, so this is the closest available substitute and it is not a substitute for an employer. AN ADMISSION IS AN ENTRY AT A PORT, not a person and not a visa: one worker travelling four times is four admissions, which is why these numbers far exceed the issuance series held separately. NEVER MIX THE TWO -- issuances count documents, admissions count arrivals, neither counts workers. STATE IS THE DESTINATION DECLARED ON ARRIVAL, usually the office being joined for a transferee; it is the nearest thing to an employer signal for these classes and it is not an employer. Figures are rounded by DHS.", "source": "DHS Office of Homeland Security Statistics, Yearbook of Immigration Statistics, nonimmigrant tables", "source_url": "https://ohss.dhs.gov/topics/immigration/yearbook", "classes": {"F1": "F-1 student", "F2": "F-2 dependant", "H1B": "H-1B specialty occupation", "H4": "H-4 dependant", "J1": "J-1 exchange visitor", "L1": "L-1 intracompany transferee", "O1": "O-1 extraordinary ability", "O2": "O-2 support", "O3": "O-3 dependant", "TN": "TN professional"}, "years": [2014, 2015, 2016, 2017, 2018, 2019, 2020, 2021, 2022, 2023], "by_class": {"F1": {"2014": 1737930, "2015": 1886950, "2016": 1892640, "2017": 1845740, "2018": 1862830, "2019": 1817720, "2020": 876160, "2021": 758460, "2022": 1199090, "2023": 1625740}, "F2": {"2014": 78220, "2015": 83000, "2016": 79440, "2017": 74460, "2018": 75340, "2019": 70290, "2020": 32460, "2021": 32310, "2022": 54730, "2023": 61910}, "H1B": {"2014": 511770, "2015": 537450, "2016": 542620, "2017": 531280, "2018": 570370, "2019": 601590, "2020": 368440, "2021": 148600, "2022": 425130, "2023": 755020}, "H4": {"2014": 184050, "201